SUMMARY:14th
LOCATION:Kendall Square Cinema\, 355 Binney St\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:Times: 12:45pm\, 6:15pm\nWritten in the wreckage of the Civil W
 ar\, the 14th Amendment was meant to close the door on the hierarchy of hu
 man worth. Instead\, it has become a permanent argument. Ava DuVernay’s 
 14th pulls this constitutional fight out of the footnotes and into the pre
 sent\, chronicling the vicious battle over the amendment that has raged fo
 r over 150 years. Threading deep archival scholarship with piercing headli
 nes of today\, 14th brings together legal minds\, politicians\, historians
  and cultural voices in direct conversation with a question America still 
 hasn’t settled: Who gets to belong?\nhttps://booking.landmarktheatres.co
 m/launch/ticketing/9d4be180-941d-5ac2-9ef6-b2e835d4d5e6\nFrom Pushpin Bost
