LOCATION:Kendall Square Cinema\, 355 Binney St\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:Times: 3:50pm\, 6:15pm\nWritten in the wreckage of the Civil Wa
 r\, the 14th Amendment was meant to close the door on the hierarchy of hum
 an worth. Instead\, it has become a permanent argument. Ava DuVernay’s 1
 4th pulls this constitutional fight out of the footnotes and into the pres
 ent\, chronicling the vicious battle over the amendment that has raged for
  over 150 years. Threading deep archival scholarship with piercing headlin
 es of today\, 14th brings together legal minds\, politicians\, historians 
 and cultural voices in direct conversation with a question America still h
 asn’t settled: Who gets to belong?\nhttps://booking.landmarktheatres.com
 /launch/ticketing/1c2d9c09-5431-5a5e-8e4a-dcb13023aebb\nFrom Pushpin Bosto
