SUMMARY:14th
LOCATION:Kendall Square Cinema\, 355 Binney St\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:Times: 2:50pm\, 5pm\nWritten in the wreckage of the Civil War\,
  the 14th Amendment was meant to close the door on the hierarchy of human 
 worth. Instead\, it has become a permanent argument. Ava DuVernay’s 14th
  pulls this constitutional fight out of the footnotes and into the present
 \, chronicling the vicious battle over the amendment that has raged for ov
 er 150 years. Threading deep archival scholarship with piercing headlines 
 of today\, 14th brings together legal minds\, politicians\, historians and
  cultural voices in direct conversation with a question America still hasn
 ’t settled: Who gets to belong?\nhttps://booking.landmarktheatres.com/la
 unch/ticketing/8f2f163b-ce1d-53ac-88c0-b8fb3dc5622c\nFrom Pushpin Boston: 
 https://pushpin.city/
